@* What this file is for: the eye button inside a password field. Clicking it shows or hides the password typed, as in the mobile app.
   How it fits in: put it right after a password <input>, inside the same box (.inp on the sign in page, .pw in dialogs). site.js does the switching. *@
<button type="button" class="pw-eye" data-show-password aria-label="Show password" title="Show password">
  <svg class="eye-on" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 12s3.5-7 10-7 10 7 10 7-3.5 7-10 7S2 12 2 12z"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/></svg>
  <svg class="eye-off" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 3l18 18"/><path d="M10.6 5.1A10.5 10.5 0 0 1 12 5c6.5 0 10 7 10 7a17.6 17.6 0 0 1-3.2 4.2M6.6 6.6C3.8 8.4 2 12 2 12s3.5 7 10 7a10 10 0 0 0 5.4-1.6"/><path d="M9.9 9.9a3 3 0 0 0 4.2 4.2"/></svg>
</button>